cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NeuralMind in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "NeuralMind: an artificial-life laboratory of spiking-neural agents"
abstract: >-
  A local-first, reproducible artificial-life world in which agents are driven
  by spiking neural networks with reward-modulated plasticity. Agents can
  perceive one another, attack, share and signal, and they can reproduce with
  mutating innate brains. The world exposes a PettingZoo ParallelEnv interface,
  so learned policies and spiking brains can be compared under identical
  rules. It ships pre-registered, multi-seed studies with committed raw
  results.
authors:
